I continued the refactor in two places. In [LRUCache.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/016_lru_cache/LRUCache.java:4), the cache now delegates all recency ordering to a dedicated `UsageList` helper at [LRUCache.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/016_lru_cache/LRUCache.java:71), which separates map concerns from linked-list mutation and makes `get`, `put`, and eviction paths much cleaner. The cache logic now reads as “lookup/update/evict,” while the list helper owns `addFirst`, `moveToFront`, `removeLast`, and `unlink`.

In [Main.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/016_lru_cache/Main.java:1), I replaced the print-only demo with a small self-checking harness that validates eviction behavior, update behavior, and constructor validation. That gives the repo an executable regression check without adding a test framework.

